WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.000
Continuum helps your AI use

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.200
what you've already figured out.

3
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.440
You've probably had conversations about

4
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.760
your work, your plans, and

5
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.920
how you like things done.

6
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.480
You've explained a problem, tried

7
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.560
an approach, and changed your

8
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.960
mind when something didn't work.

9
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.920
Then, in another conversation, you

10
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.480
find yourself explaining it again.

11
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.960
Continuum is a long-term context

12
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.480
management system.

13
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.560
That means it keeps useful

14
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.720
background from your past conversations

15
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.000
available for the work you're

16
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.440
doing now.

17
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.480
Your decisions, preferences, and lessons

18
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.640
can travel with you.

19
00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.320
Think of it as three

20
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.960
layers of memory.

21
00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.400
First, front-of-mind.

22
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.400
This is a short starting

23
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.080
page that helps your connected

24
00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.160
AI find the background it

25
00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.170
needs.

26
00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:58.690
Like the brief you'd give

27
00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:00.210
someone before they started helping

28
00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:01.650
you, it points them in

29
00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:03.410
the right direction.

30
00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:06.370
Next, remembered context.

31
00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:08.290
These are useful things drawn

32
00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.130
from your conversations:

33
00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.970
how you like to work,

34
00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.210
what you're building, and why

35
00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:16.050
you made a decision.

36
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.450
Continuum organizes them into a

37
00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:20.610
personal guide and pages about

38
00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:22.530
your different topics.

39
00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.130
You'll see the main guide

40
00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:26.530
called your constitution.

41
00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:28.370
It's a guide to understanding

42
00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:30.050
you, with references to where

43
00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:32.050
the information came from.

44
00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.450
Then, deep memory.

45
00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:36.450
This is the larger collection

46
00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.610
of conversations you can search

47
00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.450
when you need more detail.

48
00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:41.500
A decision from three years
